If a clinician starts a methadone-treatment for a patient and an initial-follow-up-period has a duration and the duration includes 1 week and a shorter-follow-up-interval contains at least 2 days and the shorter-follow-up-interval contains at most 3 days then the clinician should consider the shorter-follow-up-interval for the patient during the initial-follow-up-period.
If a clinician increases a methadone-dosage for a patient and an initial-follow-up-period has a duration and the duration includes 1 week and a shorter-follow-up-interval contains at least 2 days and the shorter-follow-up-interval contains at most 3 days then the clinician should consider the shorter-follow-up-interval for the patient during the initial-follow-up-period.
